 "slug": "forced-yes-or-no",
 "title": "Forced yes or no against \"not shown\", across models",
 "question": "Does forcing yes or no make models guess when evidence is missing, and does allowing \"not shown\" stop it?",
 "status": "shown",
 "status_note": "A later parser audit moved one count (below).",
 "summary_line": "Forced yes or no made models guess; allowing not shown nearly stopped it.",
 "headline": "Across {{F006.c.models.n}} models and {{F006.c.calls.n}} calls, Claude Opus 5.5 guessed on {{F006.c.opus_forced}} logs missing their evidence when forced, and on {{F006.c.opus_allowed}} when \"not shown\" was allowed. The {{F006.c.newer.n}} newer models pooled: {{F006.t.pooled.a}} guesses only when forced, {{F006.t.pooled.b}} only when allowed (p = {{F006.t.pooled.p}}).",
 "plain_meaning": "A forced binary answer manufactures guesses. Offering not shown removed most of them at no cost on intact logs.",
 "limits": [
  "One call per item; my items only.",
  "A guess is defined by the forced format."
 ],
